----------------------------------------------------------------------
Runtime dependencies the operator installs separately
----------------------------------------------------------------------

FFmpeg
  License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (default builds) / GPL-2.0-or-later (with
           --enable-gpl). Component licenses vary; see
           https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html.
  Why we need it: HLS segment generation, transcoding (x264 / NVENC /
                  QuickSync / VAAPI / VideoToolbox), HDR tonemap.
  How we use it: spawned as a subprocess by `apps/server/services/
                 ffmpeg_service.py`. We do not modify the FFmpeg source
                 or statically link any GPL-only component into Fluxora.
  Operator obligations: install FFmpeg from upstream
                        (https://ffmpeg.org/download.html). Fluxora does
                        not redistribute FFmpeg binaries.

mpv (libmpv) — used via the `media_kit` Flutter plugin
  License: GPL-2.0-or-later / LGPL-2.1-or-later (configurable).
  Component licenses vary; see https://mpv.io/manual/master/#copyright.
  Why we need it: video playback in the desktop and mobile clients.
  How we use it: linked at runtime via `media_kit` per-platform native
                 packages.
  Operator obligations: none beyond accepting the license terms shipped
                        with `media_kit_libs_*`.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
External services Fluxora integrates with (no code redistributed)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

TMDB — The Movie Database
  Site: https://www.themoviedb.org
  Required attribution: per TMDB's API terms, "This product uses the
  TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB." Operators who
  surface TMDB-derived metadata (poster art, descriptions) in any
  user-visible context should display the TMDB logo and the same
  notice. Fluxora's library detail panels surface TMDB-derived metadata
  to operators and any clients they pair.
  Per-tier note: the operator supplies their own TMDB API key
  (`user_settings.tmdb_api_key`). Fluxora does not proxy or pool keys.

Polar.sh — payment processor for paid tiers
  Site: https://polar.sh
  Used by: the marketing site checkout flow + the server's webhook
  handler (`apps/server/routers/webhook.py`). Fluxora does not store
  card or address data; Polar (Stripe-backed) handles all PCI-scope.
  See PRIVACY.md §3 for the data flow.

Cloudflare — Tunnel + DNS + CDN
  Site: https://www.cloudflare.com
  Used by: the marketing site (Cloudflare Pages), the optional public
  routing path for self-hosted servers (Cloudflare Tunnel), and the
  Cloudflare-anycast DoH endpoint (`https://1.1.1.1/dns-query`) used
  for the TMDB ISP-block workaround. See `docs/05_infrastructure/`.

Sentry — error reporting (opt-in)
  Site: https://sentry.io
  Used by: optional error reporting on the server. Off by default.
  Set `FLUXORA_SENTRY_DSN` to enable. See PRIVACY.md §3.5.

